  {
    "id": "90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000341",
    "value": "<p>I NCLINE to my aid, O God: O Lord, make haste to help me. Let them be confounded and ashamed: that seek after my soul. Let them be turned backward and blush for shame: that desire evils to me. Let them be presently turned away blushing for shame, that say to me: Tis well, it is well. Let all that seek You rejoice and be glad in You: and let such as love Your salvation say always, The Lord be magnified. But I am needy and poor: O God, help You me. You are my helper and my deliverer: O Lord, make no delay. Glory be to the Father, etc. V. Save Your servants: R. Trusting in You, O my God. V. Be to us, O God, a tower of strength: R. From the face of the enemy. V. Let not the enemy prevail against us: R. Nor the son of iniquity have power to hurt us. V. O Lord, deal not with us according to our sins: R. Neither reward us according to our iniquities. V. Let us pray for our chief bishop, N. R. The Lord preserve him, and give him life, and make him blessed upon earth, and deliver him not up to the will of his enemies. V. Let us pray for our benefactors: R. Vouchsafe, O Lord, for Your name's sake, to reward with eternal life all those who have done us good. V. Let us pray for the faithful departed: R. Eternal rest give to them, O Lord, and let perpetual light shine upon them. V. May they rest in peace. R. Amen. V. For our absent brethren: R. O my God, save Your servants trusting in You. V. Send them help, O Lord, from Your holy place: R. And from Sion protect them. V. O Lord, hear my prayer: R. And let my cry come to You.</p><p>Let us pray</p><p>O GOD, whose property it is always to have mercy and to spare, receive our petitions, that we, and all Your servants who are bound by the chain of sin, may, in the compassion of Your goodness, mercifully be absolved.</p><p>Hear, We urge you, O Lord, the prayer of Your suppliants, and pardon the sins of them that confess to You, that of Your bounty You may grant us pardon and peace.</p><p>Out of Your clemency, O Lord, show Your unspeakable mercy to us, that so You may both acquit us of our sins and deliver us from the punishment we deserve for them.</p><p>O God, who are offended by sin and by penance pacified, mercifully regard the prayers of Your people who make supplication to You, and turn away the scourges of Your anger, which we deserve for our sins.</p><p>O almighty and eternal God, have mercy on Your servant N., our chief bishop, and direct him, according to Your clemency, in the way of everlasting salvation, that, by Your grace, he may desire the things that are agreeable to Your will, and perform them with all his strength.</p><p>O God, from whom all holy desires, righteous counsels, and just works do come, give to Your servants that peace which the world can not give; that, our hearts being disposed to keep Your commandments, and the fear of enemies being taken away, the times, by Your protection, may be peaceable.</p><p>Inflame, O Lord, our reins and hearts with the fire of the Holy Spirit; to the end that we may serve You with a chaste body, and please You with a clean heart.</p><p>O God, the Creator and Redeemer of all the faithful, give to the souls of Your servants departed the remission of all their sins, that by pious supplications they may obtain the pardon they have always desired.</p><p>Direct, We urge you, O Lord, our actions by Your holy inspirations, and carry them on by Your gracious assistance; that every prayer and work of ours may always begin from You, and by You be happily ended.</p><p>Almighty and eternal God, who have dominion over the living and the dead, and are merciful to all whom You foreknow shall be Your by faith and good works; we humbly Urge you that they for whom we have purposed to offer our prayers, whether this present world still detains them in the flesh, or the next world has already received them divested of their bodies, may, by the clemency of Your own goodness and the intercession of Your saints, obtain pardon and full remission of all their sins. Through Our Lord Jesus Christ, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, world without end. Amen.</p><p>V. O Lord, hear my prayer. R. And let my cry come to You. V. May the almighty and merciful Lord graciously hear us. R. Amen. V. May the souls of the faithful departed through the mercy of God rest in peace. R. Amen.</p>",
    "day_number": 14
  },
